#SCADA systems 
*are the "command centres" of industrial operations. They act as the bridge between human 
operators and the machines doing the work. Think of SCADA as the nervous system of 
a factory—it senses what's happening, processes that information, and sends commands to make things happen.

TBFC uses a SCADA system to oversee its entire drone delivery operation. Without it, operators would have no 
way to monitor hundreds of drones, manage inventory, or ensure packages reach the right destinations. 
It's the invisible orchestrator of Christmas logistics.
